{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/13187","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:16.337331+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"I ran into this bug a few days ago as well! It is fixed at HEAD in XLA: https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/commit/c84f2805db56e9739c90619ea6bd6926cd20aba7. A new jaxlib release should not have this issue.","created_at":"2022-11-10T18:29:04Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/13187#issuecomment-1310730910","id":1310730910,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/13187","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5OICqe","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":1,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1310730910/reactions"},"updated_at":"2022-11-10T18:42:19Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1310730910","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1142926?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sharadmv","id":1142926,"login":"sharadmv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDI5MjY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\n\nAt [mpi4jax](https://github.com/mpi4jax/mpi4jax) we are using tokens passed to custom calls to prevent re-ordering of stateful operations. We recently noticed that we are getting wrong results when transposes are not manifested on GPU (mpi4jax/mpi4jax#176), so we tried switching to `CustomCallWithLayout`.\r\n\r\nNow to the main problem: when passing tokens to `CustomCallWithLayout`, XLA fails when trying to determine the layout of the token. (We are getting the same issue when using the new `jaxlib.mhlo_helpers.custom_call` instead.)\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef my_dummy_op_encode_cpu(ctx, x, token):\r\n    # ...\r\n    return custom_call(\r\n      b\"my_dummy_op\",\r\n      [dtype, token.type],\r\n      [x, token],\r\n      backend_config=None,\r\n      operand_layouts=[layout, ()],\r\n      result_layouts=[layout, ()],\r\n      has_side_effect=True)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis crashes the interpreter with:\r\n\r\n```\r\n 2022-11-09 19:13:37.960054: F external/org_tensorflow/tensorflow/compiler/xla/shape.h:162] Check failed: IsArray() element_type: TOKEN\r\n```\r\n\r\n[MWE on Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1qS3yE5Zav2L5XNzszWmtXJY0uaXxP0d4?usp=sharing), thanks to @EiffL.\r\n\r\nIf this is indeed a bug in XLA, is there a simple workaround? Explicitly making a copy would be acceptable as a temporary fix, but `jnp.ascontiguousarray` is not available.\n\n### What jax/jaxlib version are you using?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Which accelerator(s) are you using?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional system info\n\n_No response_\n\n### NVIDIA GPU info\n\n_No response_","closed_at":"2022-11-10T18:41:45Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/348932?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.gith